cff-version: 1.2.0
title: SARE — Safe-Reduction + Adaptive elimination ordering for sparse fill-in reduction
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. This work reports an
  evidence Level D result (correct and reproducible, without a demonstrated
  practical advantage over established baselines).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Rajve
    name: Rajve
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: https://github.com/daveaddams91-dev/sare
repository: https://github.com/daveaddams91-dev/sare
url: https://github.com/daveaddams91-dev/sare
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-19
keywords:
  - elimination ordering
  - fill-in reduction
  - sparse direct solvers
  - graph algorithms
  - verified algorithm
abstract: >-
  SARE is a deterministic adaptive elimination ordering for reducing fill-in
  in sparse direct factorization. It combines safe degree-0/1 reductions
  (provably zero fill) with an adaptive greedy phase driven by a degree /
  fill-in / lookahead potential. Correctness, zero-fill reductions, chordal
  completion, and termination are proved. Benchmarked against minimum-degree
  and minimum-fill baselines; fill is comparable but SARE is slower
  (evidence Level D).
